• Efficient OO (E-OO): denotes an interaction between a manipulated object om and a stationary background object ob that is identified as being stable, intentional, and integral to the execution of a task. This type of interaction is considered essential and is subsequently mapped into robot command primitives during plan generation. • Transitory OO (T-OO): denotes incidental interaction between a manipulated object om and a stationary background object ob that is identified as being unstable, transitory, and not representative of the core activity. These interactions are considered non-essential and are filtered out during the task segmentation process, meaning they are not translated into robot commands.
